Stop WebUI dialogs hanging off the left of a phone.

cr-dialog is 512px wide with max-width: initial. On a 377px window a
centred box wider than the screen runs off both sides, and the left side
runs off where nothing can scroll it back -- so the first character of every
label in the add-password dialog was cut off.

Adding a password is where it showed, but 512px is the shared default for
every WebUI dialog there is, so the rule goes with the default rather than
with that one dialog. Below 600px the width becomes whichever is smaller,
the dialog's own or the window less a 16px gutter each side.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

diff --git a/ui/webui/resources/cr_elements/cr_dialog/cr_dialog.css b/ui/webui/resources/cr_elements/cr_dialog/cr_dialog.css
--- a/ui/webui/resources/cr_elements/cr_dialog/cr_dialog.css
+++ b/ui/webui/resources/cr_elements/cr_dialog/cr_dialog.css
@@ -28,6 +28,18 @@
   position: absolute;
   top: 50%;
   width: var(--cr-dialog-width, 512px);
+}
+
+/* A phone. Every WebUI dialog is 512px wide with max-width: initial, which
+ * on a 377px window centres a box wider than the screen: the right side runs
+ * off, and the left side runs off where nothing can scroll it back, taking
+ * the first character of every label with it. Adding a password was the one
+ * that showed it, but the width is the shared default, so this is the shared
+ * rule rather than a fix for that dialog. */
+@media (max-width: 600px) {
+  dialog {
+    width: min(var(--cr-dialog-width, 512px), calc(100vw - 32px));
+  }
 }
 
